r2d readback zero-windows (docs/bugs-found.md final section, analysis.md 21.10):
TU_I2B_R3D=1 force all image->buffer readbacks over the 3D engine; TU_I2B_ROWS=1
force the per-row (unaligned) blit loop; TU_B2I_WFI=1 WFI after the fill (refuted);
TU_B2I_CLEAN=1 producer-side FD_CCU_CLEAN_COLOR+WFI after the fill (91/91 EXACT);
TU_I2B_SYNC=1/2/3/4 consumer-side before the readback: clean+invalidate+WFI /
invalidate only / clean only / clean without WFI (1 and 3 pass, 2 and 4 fail - the
clean and the WFI are each necessary). Plus the GDBG-i2b src-register dump. Verdict:
A7XX CP_BLIT writes land in the CCU, the public copy commands emit no cache
operations and an outside-renderpass barrier emits nothing mid-submit. Rollback:
